  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nModel guidance depicts a strong push of cold H8 air sinking \nsouthward in the late evening. Subsidence should help push some of \nthe 40-50 kt LLJ air downward resulting in gusts increasing to 45 to \n50 mph early Friday morning and persisting through most of the \ndaytime. Our upcoming rain event should help tamper down fire \nweather concerns. Winds gradually decrease in speed late Friday as \nthe H8 jet pivots to the east. Highs only warm to the 50s areawide \nunder partly to mostly cloudy skies.\n\nLate Friday night into early Saturday morning, should see a strong \n1040mb sfc high move into most of the Central and Northern Plains. \nThe light winds and clear skies should allow for us to cool \nefficiently to the low to mid 30s. Expect areas of frost to develop \nover most of the forecast area and a freeze isn't out of the \nquestion either, particularly in far northeast Nebraska.\n\nA warming trend starts for Saturday through Tuesday as 1000-500mb \nthicknesses expand over the region. Expect highs in the 60s this \nweekend, eventually hitting the 70s by Tuesday. PoPs remain less \nthan 15% during this timeframe so expect mostly dry conditions.",
